# feature-nilpy-starred-and-nested-unpacking — the DIAGNOSTIC half.
#
# `first, *rest = [1, 2, 3]` is not supported yet. Untouched it reached the
# ordinary expression-statement path and reported
#
#     error: undefined variable (first)
#
# which points at a name that is perfectly fine and reads like a typo in the
# user's own code rather than a missing feature. The form is unsupported, not
# wrong; the message has to say which.
first, *rest = [1, 2, 3]
print(first, rest)
